  "body": "Found by M5's safety re-review of #951 (2026-11-13). `fanuc-lathe.cps` `fm()` rounds a feed word to nearest, so a feed just under a rotary (C-axis live tool) cap can post up to +0.05 mm/min over it. This predates #951. #951's review asks the same of fanuc/doosan's uncapped path (judge the posted word, not the unrounded F).\n\n**Done means:** wherever a feed is held under a machine rate, the posted word is floored, or judged after rounding, so it can't exceed the rate. Pin it with a feed one rounding step under the cap.\n",
